{
  "info": {
    "name": "DropTo API \u2014 runtime regression",
    "description": "End-to-end regression run against a live DropTo API. Mutating requests stay inside the first authorized Drive root and clean up after themselves (the uploaded file and created folder are deleted at the end).\n\nRun:\n  postman collection run postman/dropto-api.postman_collection.json -e postman/local.postman_environment.json --env-var token=<accessToken cookie value>\n\nMust be run from the repo root so the upload fixture path resolves.\n\nNote: the Auth folder spends the /auth/login rate-limit budget (5 attempts / 60 s, 900 s block). Re-running inside 15 minutes answers 429 there; those three assertions accept both codes on purpose.\n\nWARNING: this collection MUTATES the storage it points at. It creates a folder and uploads a file into the FIRST authorized root, then deletes both at the end. Point it at a local API (the default baseUrl) \u2014 against production it writes into the Drive owner's real folder, and a run that fails midway leaves a `__runtime-test-<timestamp>` folder behind.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "host",
      "value": "http://127.0.0.1:4000"
    },
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://127.0.0.1:4000/api/v1"
    },
    {
      "key": "token",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "rootId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "folderId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "fileId",
      "value": ""
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Health",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "GET /health (public, off the global prefix)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('reports ok with postgres up', () => {",
                  "  const b = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(b.status).to.eql('ok');",
                  "  pm.expect(b.info.postgres.status).to.eql('up');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('responds under 1000ms', () => pm.expect(pm.response.responseTime).to.be.below(1000));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{host}}/health"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
